# armour/tiles/lames: plate lames over the plate's sleeve, thigh and greave regions (U F, T the cuisses, S the greaves)
# (P2c slice; re-cut by LADDER-ARMOUR against the owner's "pale and flat"): every third row keeps its drawn step (the
# lame's lit top edge), the two rows under it fall a step (the lame's body in its own shadow), so a vambrace, a cuisse or
# a greave reads as overlapping rigid plates with a lit rim each, never as one pale tube.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h; `on-region` is P2C_CONTRACTS 4 (the regions after the word).
use person
body adult
role overlay lames
tags tile overlay
on-region U F T S

view D key rest origin 0 0
|x
|w
|w
